      "description": "A restrained neutral composer with a single send action.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-composer\"><textarea class=\"ds-question\" aria-label=\"Ask Bellwether\" placeholder=\"Ask about firms, people, or opportunities...\" rows=\"2\"></textarea><div class=\"ds-compose-foot\"><span>Bellwether AI</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-compose-send\">Ask</button></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-composer{font-family:var(--sans,\"Instrument Sans\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif);background:#222222;border:1px solid #494949;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 20px;}.ds-composer:focus-within{border-color:#888;}.ds-question{font-family:var(--sans,\"Instrument Sans\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif);display:block;width:100%;min-height:70px;padding:0;border:0;background:none;color:var(--ink,#f0f0f0);resize:none;font-size:15px;}.ds-question::placeholder{color:var(--faint,#a0a0a0);opacity:1;}.ds-question:focus,.ds-question:focus-visible{outline:none;box-shadow:none;}.ds-compose-foot{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-top:12px;color:var(--faint,#a0a0a0);font-size:11px;}.ds-compose-send{font-family:var(--sans,\"Instrument Sans\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;min-height:40px;padding:9px 15px;border:1px solid var(--rule2,#4a4a4a);border-radius:8px;font-size:13px;font-weight:550;line-height:1.3;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none;transition:border-color .12s,background .12s;background:var(--red,#b73545);color:#fff;border-color:transparent;font-weight:600;}.ds-compose-send:hover{background:var(--red-hover,#9f2c3b);}.ds-compose-send:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--red-hi,#ef939c);outline-offset:3px;}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-compose-send{transition:none;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Intelligence Workspace",
    "overview": "Bellwether is a serious, neutral charcoal workspace in which firm identity, evidence and available actions are easy to scan. Restrained red supplies emphasis; hierarchy comes from type, spacing, thin borders and deliberate disclosure. The interface carries substantial information without making every fact compete in the first view.\n\nThe approved identity is the open geometric B with its red signal point, paired with a sans-serif wordmark. The self-hosted Instrument Sans is intentional. Preserve the professional, restrained character confirmed in PRODUCT.md: neutral dark grey surfaces, room to read, and a quiet sign-in experience.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral charcoal layers with restrained red emphasis.",
      "Readable identity and evidence before secondary detail.",
      "Flat panels, fine rules and compact rectangular controls.",
      "Progressive disclosure with complete routes to every workflow.",
      "Clear distinctions between verified, unknown and missing evidence."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Signal Rule",
        "body": "Use red for an action, selected state or meaningful status; keep large backgrounds neutral.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Rule",
        "body": "Pair semantic color with explicit labels and values. Missing evidence remains visibly different from a known negative or a verified fact.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Keep Instrument Sans across headings, body and controls; express hierarchy with size, weight and spacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Progressive Disclosure Rule",
        "body": "Keep identity, current evidence and the next action visible; put secondary filters, sources and management fields behind a clearly named control.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Workspace Rule",
        "body": "Establish depth through tone and borders; reserve floating elevation for temporary overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep major surfaces neutral charcoal and let red identify purposeful interaction.",
      "**Do** retain the geometric B asset and self-hosted Instrument Sans.",
      "**Do** disclose secondary detail while keeping every supported workflow reachable.",
      "**Do** pair scores and contact states with visible evidence or uncertainty.",
      "**Do** preserve visible keyboard focus and respect reduced-motion preferences.",
      "**Do** reflow identity and action groups before reducing text or squeezing columns."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** introduce blue-tinted surfaces, theatrical login graphics, halos or oversized AI ornaments.",
      "**Don't** use decorative eyebrow labels, gratuitous glyph icons or a separate system display face.",
      "**Don't** replace unknown values with invented data or present inferred email addresses as usable contacts.",
      "**Don't** spread shadows, accent fills or nested cards across routine workspace content.",
      "**Don't** use residual legacy CSS or isolated view-specific defects as rules for new screens."
    ]
  }
